Depends: nodejs (>= 22), adduser, debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0
Description: Headless daemon for Ötzi threshold signing
 otzi-headless is a daemon variant of Ötzi for automated and federated
 threshold-signing systems (bridge reserves, liquidity pools, multi-party
 server vaults). Machine-triggered ML-DSA + FROST ceremonies over OPNet
 Bitcoin L1.
 .
 The daemon is a signing backend for critical-infrastructure keys: it
 holds threshold-shared key material across a ring of trust and signs
 what authorized operators POST to its HTTP API. Triggers, chain
 watching, and decision logic live in operator infrastructure.
